<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eugenia Charles</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a>–<a href="/years/2005">2005</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eugenia Charles was a Dominican lawyer and leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominica-freedom-party">Dominica Freedom Party</a> who served as prime minister from 1980 to 1995, the first woman to head a government in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. She survived coup plots in 1981 and, as chair of the Organisation of Eastern Caribbean States, supported the United States-led invasion of Grenada in 1983.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eugenia-charles.jpg" alt="Eugenia Charles" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gotfryd, Bernard, photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eugenia_Charles_at_the_United_Nations.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
